{"t":1788460712,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"eeb3c5db-1a82-44b7-a6d6-4427de03116b","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-09-03T15:57:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 031557\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n1157 AM EDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nTrimmed away more of the Heat Advisory due to continued cloud\ncover. Monitoring shower and thunderstorm potential for later.\n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Slight Risk of severe thunderstorms today and Friday.\n\n- 2) Hot and humid conditions will persist through Friday.\n\n- 3) Drier conditions expected for the Labor Day weekend ahead.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Slight Risk of severe thunderstorms today and\nFriday.\n\nMultiple thunderstorm clusters will move from Pennsylvania east\nsoutheast through tonight along a frontal zone well defined on \nsurface observations and recent NUCAPS data. Given hot and \nunstable air mass south of this frontal zone and moderately \nstrong flow aloft, thunderstorms will be capable of producing \ndamaging wind gusts.\n\nA lot of uncertainty remains in timing and magnitude of\nconvection given recent CAMs haven't handled the extent of \nmorning showers and storms very well. General thought is that\nareas along and near the baroclinic zone left in the wake of\nprior convection will continue to see waves of showers and\nthunderstorms over the next 24 to 48 hours, with a gradual\nprogression south and west with each passing round.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Hot and humid conditions will persist through\nFriday.\n\nHave cancelled most of the Heat Advisory given lots of upstream\nclouds and convection. It will still be hot and humid nonetheless.\nSimilar heat indices are expected Friday.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nAs the cold front from earlier in the week tracks south of the \nregion, surface high pressure begins to move across the Great Lakes \nSaturday. Mid-level dry air settles over the Mid-Atlantic between \nSaturday and Sunday, allowing for heat & humidity to drop through \nthe weekend. Highs for Sunday range in the low 80s across much of \nthe area, with dewpoints ranging in the 50s and low-60s. Overall, it \nshould feel relatively mild & dry over the Labor Day holiday. \n\nThunderstorm chances drop during this period as well with \nincreasingly stable conditions. Looking towards early next week, \nupper-level ridging will begin to build over the Appalachians, \nallowing for relatively dry conditions to continue as temperatures \nstart to increase again by Tuesday. Thunderstorm chances remain low \nas this ridging builds overhead into next week.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /15Z THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nNumerous thunderstorms expected today and Fri, some of which, \ncould be severe with damaging winds. Exact timing remains \nuncertain and will continue to handle TAFs with long PROB30 \ngroups until things become clearer. \n\nPrevailing VFR conditions are anticipated at terminals through \nSunday & Monday. Northeast winds shift southeasterly by Monday \nevening.\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nSMWs may be needed again today especially north of the US-50\nbridge and everywhere Friday.\n\nWind gusts stay below 15 knots between Sunday and Monday. Northeast \nwinds shift southeasterly by Monday evening.\n\n&&\n\n.CLIMATE...\nA record daily high minimum of 73 degrees occurred at IAD \nyesterday Wed Sep 02. This broke the old record of 72 degrees\nset in 2020.\n\nRecord daily high maximums are not expected today or Friday as\nrecords are in the upper 90s to low 100s. However, record daily\nhigh minimums are still possible, but not likely, since\nwidespread convection is expected that should bring \ntemperatures close to their dewpoints.\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...None.\nVA...Heat Advisory until 7 PM EDT this evening for VAZ036-037.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...None.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...LFR/DHOF/SRT\nAVIATION...LFR/DHOF/SRT\nMARINE...LFR/DHOF/SRT\n"},"forecast":{"t":1788460649,"days":{"2026-09-03":{"hi":95,"lo":76,"pop":40,"short":"Isolated Showers And Thunderstorms"},"2026-09-04":{"hi":92,"lo":73,"pop":53,"short":"Mostly Sunny then Slight Chance Showers And Thunderstorms"},"2026-09-05":{"hi":85,"lo":66,"pop":27,"short":"Chance Rain Showers"},"2026-09-06":{"hi":83,"lo":64,"pop":6,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-09-07":{"hi":82,"lo":64,"pop":2,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-09-08":{"hi":85,"lo":65,"pop":1,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-09-09":{"hi":88,"lo":72,"pop":13,"short":"Mostly Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1788458400,"n":48,"ceil":[10000,null,null,null,null,10000,10000,9800,10000,10000,10000,10000,10000,9700,9900,8200,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,6700,5300,4000,4200,4300,8600,4500,4500,3600,null,3600,4300,null,null,null,3600,3600,5300,5300,5300,null,null,null],"vis":[10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,9.0,7.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0,10.0],"spd":[5,5,5,5,4,4,4,3,3,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,4,4,5,5,6,6,6,6,5,4,3,2,2,2,2,2,3,3,3,4,4,4,5,5,5,6,6,5],"gst":[9,9,9,9,8,7,7,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,5,5,6,6,6,7,8,9,10,10,9,9,8,7,6,5,6,6,7,6,7,8,8,8,9,9,9,10,10,10,9,9],"dir":[250,250,260,260,260,230,210,210,210,230,270,250,250,280,250,240,270,290,290,290,290,300,300,300,300,300,300,290,300,280,290,270,310,300,300,310,310,320,340,340,0,10,20,20,20,10,10,0],"pop":[17,17,16,22,28,27,27,33,42,43,38,37,37,31,13,7,8,6,8,8,8,8,16,14,20,25,43,51,45,46,41,46,52,49,35,43,7,5,5,7,10,9,10,10,10,10,10,10],"temp":[33.3,33.3,33.3,32.8,32.2,31.1,28.9,27.2,26.7,26.1,25.6,25,25,25,24.4,24.4,24.4,23.9,25.6,27.2,28.9,30,31.1,32.2,32.8,32.8,32.2,31.7,31.1,30,27.8,26.7,25.6,25,24.4,23.9,23.9,23.3,23.3,22.8,22.2,22.2,23.3,25,26.1,26.7,27.8,28.3],"dew":[23.3,23.3,23.3,22.8,22.8,22.8,23.3,23.3,22.8,22.8,22.8,22.8,22.2,22.2,22.2,22.